            "title": "Crypto's connections to the rest of the financial system",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "PARIS (Reuters) -Cryptocurrency markets have surged in recent years, in part fuelled by the Trump administration's pro-crypto stance which has encouraged wider acceptance among financial institutions.  With a total value of $3.2 trillion and around $197 billion of trading volume per day, cryptocurrencies represent \u200ba small part of global markets, crypto tracker CoinGecko estimates.  But regulators and investors are still worried about whether any problems in the lightly regulated crypto world \u200ccould spill over into the wider financial system.",
